"/us/en/acute-care/proclinical": {"template":"tier2-landing-page","metadata":{"title":"ProClinical","pageTitle":null,"description":"At Stryker, we recognize the strain these challenges place on care teams and their potential impact on patient outcomes. ProClinical provides clinical experts that help prioritize people, elevate your products, optimize your processes and leverage timely data for a comprehensive approach to drive better patient outcomes.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/acute-care/proclinical/images/proclinical_targeted-solutions_secondary-hero_1200x680.jpg","imageAlt":"Stryker's ProClinical team discussing data insights with hospital medical staff.","tags":[],"originallyPublished":"2024-08-20T19:50:28.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-03-30T14:33:26.000Z","contentID":"AC-ACCL-SYK-1198622_REV-1_en_us"},"anchors":[{"id":"contact-us","title":"Contact Us","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"product-info","title":"Product Information","hidden":false,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p>1. Peng D, Ye Y, et al. Journal of Operations Management. The impact of nurse staffing on turnover and quality: An empirical examination of nursing care within hospital units. March 26, 2023. Retrieved May 16, 2024.<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>2. Intensive care unit nurse demographics and statistics in the US. www.zippia.com. Retrieved May 16, 2024.</p>","forms":[{"formId":"2761","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank you for your interest. A Stryker representative will reach out to you shortly.","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[],"missingAlt":[]},
"/us/en/acute-care/products/fall-prevention-solutions": {"template":"tier2-landing-page","metadata":{"title":"Fall Prevention Solutions","pageTitle":null,"description":"Stryker’s connected ProCuity beds and Prime Connect stretchers can help with your hospital's fall prevention strategies. ","image":"/content/dam/stryker/acute-care/products/fall-prevention/fall-prevention-hero_1200x680.jpg","imageAlt":"nurse looking back toward patient getting out of hospital bed","tags":["stryker:product/acute-care/fall-prevention-solutions"],"originallyPublished":"2023-02-06T21:42:45.000Z","lastPublished":"2025-02-06T01:24:47.000Z","contentID":"AC-GSNPS-SYK-1190425_REV-1_en_us"},"anchors":[{"id":"overview","title":"Overview","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"connect","title":"Connect","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"resources","title":"Resources","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p>*Requires ProCuity and/or Prime Connect to be integrated with Vocera Engage intelligent middleware through our wireless system. Vocera Engage includes Engage Medical Device Alarm Notification (EMDAN), FDA 510(k)-cleared middleware, to deliver secondary alarms. Capabilities are based on your facility’s protocols and technology configuration.</p>\r\n<p>**Requires integration with our wireless system.</p>\r\n<p>†These hospitals’ results reflect the policies, protocols, technology and training implemented by these hospitals and the results are not necessarily representative of what another hospital may experience. </p>\r\n<p>1. Health Research &amp; Educational Trust. Preventing patient falls: A systematic approach from the Joint Commission Center for Transforming Healthcare project. Oct 2016. Retrieved June 30, 2023.</p>\r\n<p>2. Assisted and Unassisted Falls: Different Events, Different Outcomes, Different Implications for Quality of Hospital Care. Jt Comm J Qual Patient Saf. 2014 August; 40(8): 358–364. Accessed 30 June 2023. Retrieved June 30, 2023.</p>\r\n<p>3. Falls. Patient Safety Network. September 7, 2018. Retrieved July 1, 2024.</p>\r\n<p>4. Dykes PC,&nbsp;Burns Z,&nbsp;Adelman J, et al. Evaluation of a Patient-Centered Fall-Prevention Tool Kit to Reduce Falls and Injuries:&nbsp;A Nonrandomized Controlled Trial.&nbsp;<i>JAMA Netw Open.</i>&nbsp;2020;3(11):e2025889. doi:10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2020.25889. Retrieved July 1, 2024.</p>\r\n<p>5. Rohac, Delane, et al. Outcomes Story: Targeted Fall Prevention Interventions and Wireless Technology Results in Successful Quality Improvement Intervention. October 2018. Retrieved July 1, 2024.</p>\r\n<p>6. Cook NS, Komansky BJ, Urton MS. Do No Harm: A Multifactorial Approach to Preventing Emergency Department Falls – A Quality Improvement Project. J Emerg Nurs. 2020 Sep;46(5):666-674. doi: 10.1016/j.jen.2020.03.007. Epub 2020 Jun 4. PMID: 32507724. Retrieved July 1, 2024.</p>","forms":[{"formId":"2761","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank you for your interest. A Stryker representative will reach out to you shortly.","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[["Related Products","News Articles"]],"cardLists":[{"component":"customizable","title":"Related products","items":[{"path":"/us/en/acute-care/products/prime-series","resolved":true,"title":"Prime Series","description":"Our Prime Series stretchers are designed to reduce physical strain on clinicians, enhance comfort during patient transport and drive hospital efficiency.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/acute-care/products/primeseries/images/20200708-Stryker_Surfaces-31.png","alt":"Prime electric hospital transport gurney"},{"path":"/us/en/acute-care/products/procuity/","resolved":false},{"path":"/us/en/acute-care/dynamic-clinical-workflow","resolved":true,"title":"Dynamic Clinical Workflow","description":"Bring together the people and information you need to deliver quality patient care with our adaptable, scalable platform.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/acute-care/campaigns/dynamic-clinical-workflow/dcw-launch-hero_1200x680.jpg","alt":"two hospital beds, mobile and and wearable devices"}]},{"component":"customizable_copy","title":null,"items":[{"path":"/us/en/acute-care/products/vocera-engage","resolved":false},{"path":"/us/en/acute-care/products/vocera-smartbadge","resolved":false},{"path":"/us/en/acute-care/products/vocera-minibadge","resolved":false}]},{"component":"customizable","title":null,"items":[{"path":"/us/en/acute-care/news/ibed-fall-prevention-clinical-outcome","resolved":true,"title":"Abstract: Quality Improvement Initiative Incorporates iBed Technology into Fall Prevention Bundle of Care","description":"This clinical outcome story addresses the pressing concern of accidental falls in acute care settings, attributing them to multifaceted factors such as patient physiology, staff behavior and hospital environment. This piece discusses how regular safety audits were employed to bolster compliance with fall prevention strategies and foster a culture of safety.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/acute-care/products/ibedwireless/images/iBed_Wireless_Bed-Exit_Red_666x392.jpg","alt":"patient falling out of bed with red alert light on"},{"path":"/us/en/acute-care/news/hospital-bed-standardization-va","resolved":true,"title":"VA hospitals: enabling bed standardization while supporting SCI patient communication","description":"Delivering quality care that helps Veterans achieve the best possible health outcomes, in a way that is safe and efficient for the nurses and staff who provide patient care, is vitally important. We are honored to work with many VA hospitals across the country as partners in prevention, together creating a better healthcare experience for care teams and patients.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/acute-care/news/bed-standardization-in-va-hospitals/nurse-smiling-at-patient-in-bed_1200x675.jpg","alt":"nurse smiling at patient in bed"}]}],"missingAlt":[]},
