"/us/en/emergency-care/hospitals-clinics": {"template":"tier2-landing-page","metadata":{"title":"Hospitals and clinics","pageTitle":"Hospitals and clinics","description":"Our emergency medical solutions are built for consistency, clinical clarity and confidence. Because during cardiac and emergent events, code teams don’t just respond – they lead.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/ems/hospitals-clinics/images/prime-x_LUCAS-3_lifepak-35_hospital-corridor_1200x680.jpg","imageAlt":"Three nurses wheeling patient down hospital corridor on Prime-X stretcher being treated with LIFEPAK-35 and LUCAS-3","tags":["stryker:business-unit/ems"],"originallyPublished":"2023-02-06T14:59:07.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-08-19T21:27:28.000Z","contentID":"AC-GSNPS-SYK-1190955_REV-1_en_us"},"anchors":[{"id":"care-system","title":"Overview","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"products","title":"Products","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"services","title":"Services","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"contact","title":"contact","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"resources","title":"Resources","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p>1.&nbsp;Data on file, Stryker LIFEPAK CR2 OI 3349335-00. </p>\r\n<p>2. Data on file, Stryker LIFENET 3347969_K. </p>\r\n<p>3. Data on file, Stryker OI 3337705-008. </p>\r\n<p>4. Beesems SG, Hardig BM, Nilsson A, Koster RW, Force and depth of mechanical chest compressions and their relation to chest height and gender in an out-of-hospital setting, Resuscitation, 2015;91:67-72.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>5. Data on file, Stryker LIFEPAK 35 Human Factors Validation Report, 3338373, Appendix B.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>6.&nbsp;Data on file, Stryker LIFENET LCCRD 3349947.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>7. Data on file, Stryker LIFENET LCCRD 3347969. </p>\r\n<p>8. Pocock H, Deakin C, Quinn T, et al. Human factors in prehospital research: Lessons from the Paramedic trial. Emergency Medical Journal. 2016;33(8):562-8.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>9. Data on file, Stryker CR2 Usability Validation Report 3319528.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>10. Data on file, Stryker LUCAS 3 IFU 101034-00 Rev J.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>11. Data on file, Stryker SHVR 3338410.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>12. Becker L, Zaloshnja E, Levick N, et al. Relative risk of injury and death in ambulances and other emergency vehicles. Accident analysis and prevention. 2003;35(6): 941-48.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>13. Jones A, Lee R. Cardiopulmonary resuscitation and back injury in ambulance officers. International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health. 2005 May;78 (4); 332-36.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>14. Edelson, et al. Interim guidance for basic and advanced life support in adults, children, and neonates with suspected or confirmed COVID-19. Circulation. 2020.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>","forms":[{"formId":"1322","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thanks!","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[{"component":"customizable","title":null,"items":[{"path":"/us/en/emergency-care/news/2025/enhancing-pediatric-advanced-life-support","resolved":true,"title":"Enhancing pediatric advanced life support: A tool for lifesaving care","description":"The LIFEPAK 35 monitor/defibrillator was designed to support pediatric resuscitation and advanced care, helping clinicians respond with precision in critical moments.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/ems/news/images/ec-newsroom_pediatric-technology_thumbnail_1440x816.jpg","alt":"Students walking in school hallway"},{"path":"/us/en/emergency-care/news/2023/understanding-the-basics-of-a-lucas-chest-compression-system","resolved":true,"title":"Understanding the basics of a LUCAS chest compression system","description":"When it comes to medical emergencies like sudden cardiac arrest, time is of the essence. Traditional cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) can be demanding and fatiguing, even for first responders. This is where a LUCAS chest compression system comes into play. The innovative LUCAS device offers a viable solution for consistent, high-quality chest compressions, a critical component in resuscitation.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/ems/images/Increased efficiencies.jpg","alt":"LUCAS device placed on a sudden cardiac arrest victim "},{"path":"/us/en/emergency-care/news/2022/help-increase-patient-outcomes-both-in-and-out-of-the-hospital","resolved":true,"title":"Help increase patient outcomes both in and out of the hospital","description":null,"image":"/content/dam/stryker/ems/news/images/cprINSIGHT article thumbnail.jpg","alt":"Bystander using a LIFEPAK CR2 AED on a sudden cardiac arrest vicitim in a public setting "}]}],"missingAlt":[]},
