"/us/en/joint-replacement/products/dual-mobility": {"template":"tier2-landing-page","metadata":{"title":"Dual Mobility","pageTitle":"Dual Mobility","description":"Stryker is committed to being your Dual Mobility provider of choice. ​","image":"/content/dam/stryker/joint-replacement/images/Screenshot 2025-10-02 103249.png","imageAlt":"modular dual mobility offerings","tags":["stryker:content-type/product","stryker:business-unit/joint-replacement","stryker:product/joint-replacement/dual-mobility","stryker:portfolio/orthopaedics","stryker:specialty/hip-joint-replacement","stryker:capability/joint-replacement","stryker:content-type/hcp_content"],"originallyPublished":"2025-10-09T20:30:14.000Z","lastPublished":"2025-10-13T18:40:26.000Z","contentID":"JR-GSNPS-SYK-2264254"},"anchors":[{"id":"product","title":"Product offerings","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"benefits","title":"Key benefits","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"resources","title":"Resources","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"contact","title":"Request more info","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p>References:&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li><p>Dubin JA, Westrich GH. Lack of early dislocation for dual mobility vs. fixed bearing total hip arthroplasty: A multi-center analysis of comparable cohorts. J Orthop. 2020;21:1-5. doi:10.1016/j.jor.2020.02.006​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><p>Guyen O. Hemiarthroplasty or total hip arthroplasty in recent femoral neck fractures? Orthop Traumatol Surg Res. 2019 Feb;105(1S):S95-S101. doi: 10.1016/j.otsr.2018.04.034. Epub 2018 Nov 16. PMID: 30449680.​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><p>Li WT, Kozick Z, Sherman M, Restrepo C, Smith EB, Courtney PM. Dual mobility bearing articulations result in lower rates of dislocation after revision total hip arthroplasty. J Am Acad Orthop Surg. Accepted manuscript. Published online December 4, 2019. doi:10.5435/JAAOS-D-19-00532. doi:10.5435/JAAOS-D-19-00532​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><p>MDM and Novae jump distance comparison​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><p>Stryker Internal Technical Memo A0012226. 2D Jump Distance comparison for MDM and G7. March 2016. ​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><p>Stryker Internal Technical Memo D0000055054. 2D Jump Distance comparison for MDM and OR3O. July 2020.​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><p>Stryker Internal Data on File. 2024.​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><p>Batailler C, Lustig S, Balot E, Farizon F, Fessy MH, Philippot R. Ten to 15-Year Outcomes of Monoblock Uncemented Dual Mobility Cups: Excellent Survival Rate and Outcome in Primary Total Hip Arthroplasty. JB JS Open Access. 2025 Feb 21;10(1):e24.00074. doi: 10.2106/JBJS.OA.24.00074. PMID: 39991112; PMCID: PMC11841846.​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><p>Remily EA, Douglas SJ, Sax OC, Pervaiz SS, Mohamed NS, Wilkie WA, Smith LS, Nace J, Malkani AL, Jaggard CE, Kolisek FR, Delanois RE. Sequentially Irradiated and Annealed Highly Cross-Linked Polyethylene: Linear Vector and Volumetric Wear in Total Hip Arthroplasty at 10 Years. Arthroplast Today. 2021 Sep 9;11:140-145. doi: 10.1016/j.artd.2021.08.002. PMID: 34541267; PMCID: PMC8435938.​</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>","forms":[{"formId":"4107","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank You! ","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[],"missingAlt":[]},
