"/us/en/sage/c/journey-to-zero": {"template":"tier2-landing-page","metadata":{"title":"Journey to Zero","pageTitle":"Journey to Zero healthcare worker injuries","description":"The Journey to Zero program can help create a culture of safety that benefits your patients, nurses, and your organization. The program offers products and services to help improve safe patient handling and nurse safety while addressing staffing issues.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/sage/journey-to-zero/Sage-Journey-to-Zero-nurse-back-injury.jpg","imageAlt":"Nurse experiencing back pain.","tags":[],"originallyPublished":"2023-02-06T21:54:47.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-08-20T19:52:19.000Z","contentID":"SAGE-PVN-WEB-498450_REV-0_en_us"},"anchors":[{"id":"contact-us","title":"Start the journey","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p><b>References: 1.</b> American Nurses Association, Position Statement: Safe Patient Handling Movement. Retrieved from http://nursingworld.org/DocumentVault/GOVA/Federal/Federal-Issues/SPHM.html. Accessed July 19, 2017 <b>2.</b> American Nurse Today, Special Report: Preventing Patient-Handling Injuries in Nurses, 2016;11(5):37-44. <b>3.</b> 2021 NSI National Health Care Retention &amp; RN Staffing Report, Nursing Solutions, Inc. March, 2021. <b>4.</b> Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA), Worker Safety in Your Hospital brochure, 2013.</p>\r\n<p>Zero healthcare worker injuries and zero doubt messages are not guarantees and are aspirational in nature.</p>","forms":[{"formId":"1259","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank you! We received your information and a Stryker Sage representative will be in contact.","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[],"missingAlt":[]},
