"/us/en/sports-medicine/c/rotator_cuff_repair_solutions": {"template":"tier2-landing-page","metadata":{"title":"Rotator cuff repair solutions","pageTitle":"Rotator cuff repair solutions","description":"Our rotator cuff repair portfolio offers versatile solutions for a range of pathologies. From the hydroxyapatite and bioglass-coated Iconix HA+ to the minimally-invasive InSpace subacromial balloon spacer and knotless options like Iconix Knotless and AlphaVent Knotless, we deliver technologies designed to address the complexities of partial, full-thickness and massive irreparable rotator cuff repairs (RCTs).","image":null,"imageAlt":"rotator-cuff-repair-","tags":["stryker:procedure/sports-medicine","stryker:business-unit/sports-medicine","stryker:specialty/shoulder-sports-med","stryker:custom/sports-medicine/procedure-(shoulder)","stryker:product/sports-medicine","stryker:custom/sports-medicine/procedure/rotator-cuff-repair","stryker:custom/sports-medicine/procedure-(shoulder)/rotator-cuff-repair","stryker:procedure/sports-medicine/rotator-cuff-repair"],"originallyPublished":"2025-12-02T18:52:15.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-08-19T17:02:50.000Z","contentID":"SM-GSNPS-SYK-1912588"},"anchors":[{"id":"product-solutions","title":"Stryker’s solutions for Rotator Cuff","hidden":false,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"video-solutions","title":"Videos","hidden":false,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"connect-form","title":"Connect with us","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p>*Instrumentation is available for preparation of a pilot hole if required.</p>\r\n<p>**Stryker consultant</p>\r\n<p>References</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Rashid MS, Cooper C, Cook J, Cooper D, Dakin SG, Snelling S, Carr AJ. Increasing age and tear size reduce rotator cuff repair healing rate at 1 year. Acta Orthop. 2017 Dec;88(6):606-611. doi: 10.1080/17453674.2017.1370844. Epub 2017 Sep 7. PMID: 28880113; PMCID: PMC5694804.</li>\r\n<li>Verma N, Srikumaran U, Roden CM, Rogusky EJ, Lapner P, Neill H, Abboud JA; on behalf of the SPACE GROUP. InSpace Implant Compared with Partial Repair for the Treatment of Full-Thickness Massive Rotator Cuff Tears: A Multicenter, Single-Blinded, Randomized Controlled Trial. J Bone Joint Surg Am. 2022 Jul 20;104(14):1250-1262. doi: 10.2106/JBJS.21.00667. Epub 2022 Apr 25. PMID: 35777921.</li>\r\n<li>Stryker DHFD15515 1000904424 Rev A</li>\r\n<li>RiverPoint Medical VP-65C</li>\r\n<li>Stryker DHD14024</li>\r\n<li>Applies to 1.4mm anchor. Product specifications are derived from publicly accessible websites of the legal manufacturers and/or physical measurements as of July 2025.</li>\r\n</ol>","forms":[{"formId":"3149","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank you! We have received your request. A Stryker representative will be in contact with you soon.","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[],"missingAlt":[]},
